Arne Anka <mats.sparr@mailbox.swipnet.se> wrote:

>Is it possible to write an OPL (OPA) that is running in the
>background and goes active and does some action when i
>turn my psion off?

Yes, capture the OFF key with the following code:

IF CALL($C58D, 8195, 3592) AND 255
	ALERT("Error: can not capture OFF key")
	STOP
ENDIF

In your event-loop an event with a keycode 8195 is generated:

LOCAL	sysmsg%, keycode%, keymod%
WHILE 1
	IOA(-1,14,sysmsg%,keycode%,#0) rem wait for event
	IOWAIT
	...
	IF sysmsg <> -46
		...
		IF keycode% = 8195
			doSomething:
		ENDIF
		...
	ENFIF
	...
ENDWH



